                             Zeus LastCallers

                                   v1.8

                            ©1996 by Rod Schnell


Description
~~~~~~~~~~~
A Zdoor that shows who the last callers were, along with some general
interest system information. Credit is given to Kevin Gearing for the look
of this door, which is quite similar to an Arexx door written by him. 


Features
~~~~~~~~
  - Zdoor
  - Gets the lastcaller information directly from Zeus' lastcaller list in
    memory.
  - Displays a lastcallers list for all lines in reverse chronological order,
    with currently online users at the top.
  - Supports the user's screen height to fill the screen with information.
  - Has options to use realnames or handles, show sysop logons and show local
    logons.
  - C source code is included.


Usage
~~~~~
Note - If you (the sysop) have a habit of logging on and off continually and
       have Zeus configured to keep a small last callers lists, then you might
       be the only one in it. If you find the list isn't filling the screen or
       often contains nothing but local sysop calls all you need do is
       reconfigure Zeus to keep a longer list. Keeping a list of 100 callers
       is suggested.

  10 LastCallers is a Zdoor, taking one required argument (the linenumber)
  and 3 optional arguments.

	Syntax: LastCallers <LINENUMBER> [REALNAMES] [SHOWSYSOP] [SHOWLOCAL]
	
  LINENUMBER - Required argument that *MUST* be the first argument.

  The other 3 arguments are switches that may be given in any order.

  REALNAMES  - Show callers realnames. If this switch is not given handles
               will be shown instead.
  SHOWSYSOP  - Show sysop logons (checks user name against sysop name). If
               this argument is not given sysop logons won't be shown.
  SHOWLOCAL  - Show local logons, if not given, local logons won't be shown.
  


Installation
~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Installation is easy, simply copy LastCallers to Doors: and run it from
  anywhere you like.

  Different ways to run it...

      ZDoor '"LastCallers 'Line'"'
      ZDoor '"LastCallers 'Line' REALNAMES"'
      ZDoor '"LastCallers 'Line' SHOWSYSOP"'
      ZDoor '"LastCallers 'Line' SHOWLOCAL "'
      ZDoor '"LastCallers 'Line' SHOWLOCAL REALNAMES"'
      ZDoor '"LastCallers 'Line' SHOWSYSOP SHOWLOCAL "'
      ZDoor '"LastCallers 'Line' SHOWSYSOP REALNAMES "'
      ZDoor '"LastCallers 'Line' SHOWSYSOP SHOWLOCAL REALNAMES"'

  Example menu entry...
  
    Option_L:
      RIPReset
      ZDoor '"LastCallers 'Line'"'
      Signal MenuLoop


History
~~~~~~~
  v1.0 - First version, released 04-Mar-96.
  v1.1 - Recompiled as pure, residentable program.
       - Optimized for a smaller, faster executeable.
       - Online users are now shown at top of list.
       - Added support for user's screenlength, shows as many last callers as
         will fit on one screen.
       - Added some color to user information display, making it easier to
         read.
       - Title changed from "10 Last Callers" to "Last Callers".
       - Released 14-Mar-96 with source code included.
  v1.2 - Bugfix, now shows users on the highest line number too.
       - Minior code optimizations.
  v1.3 - Now shows user his own line irregardless of SHOWSYSOP/SHOWLOCAL
         settings.
  v1.4 - Released 28-Apr-96
       - Bugfix for small screen heights (less than 15), some strange things
         could happen. Bug reported by Vacu.
       - Minimum number of callers displayed is now 10 regardless of screen
         height.
       - Changed to only leave one blank line at bottom of screen (used to
         be 3).
  v1.5 - Changed internal screen clearing/positioning code so ESC[H won't be
         sent if user has screen clearing codes turned off.
  v1.6 - Added forced screen clear, screen clear will be sent regardless of
         user's clrscr settings.
  v1.7 - Minor changes made to header title text (03-Sep-96).
  v1.8 - Oops! Just realized there's a semaphore controlling access to the
         last callers list. Added code to use it. (08-Sep-96)


